{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1535","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Array Reodering"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given an array $$$a$$$ consisting of $$$n$$$ integers."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's call a pair of indices $$$i$$$, $$$j$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if $$$1 \\le i \\lt j \\le n$$$ and $$$\\gcd(a_i, 2a_j) \\gt 1$$$ (where $$$\\gcd(x, y)$$$ is the greatest common divisor of $$$x$$$ and $$$y$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Find the maximum number of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" index pairs if you can reorder the array $$$a$$$ in an arbitrary way."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 1000$$$) — the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the test case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$2 \\le n \\le 2000$$$) — the number of elements in the array."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of the test case contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\dots, a_n$$$ ($$$1 \\le a_i \\le 10^5$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$2000$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output a single integer — the maximum number of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" index pairs if you can reorder the array $$$a$$$ in an arbitrary way."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n4\n3 6 5 3\n2\n1 7\n5\n1 4 2 4 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n0\n9\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example, the array elements can be rearranged as follows: $$$[6, 3, 5, 3]$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third example, the array elements can be rearranged as follows: $$$[4, 4, 2, 1, 1]$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"1535B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1535/problem/B"}